# MediaArchivistBot Project Context

Before making changes, read and follow `AGENTS.md` and relevant sections of
`README.md`.

Core constraints:

- Keep all repository and bot-facing text in English.
- Preserve bilingual English/Russian retrieval aliases.
- Keep controversial-content indexing factual, uncensored, and non-moralizing.
- Private search must verify live membership and filter chats before ranking.
- Group search is restricted to the current chat.
- Inline search is membership-scoped across shared groups; Telegram inline
  queries do not provide the current chat id.
- Never index media authored by this bot or sent through this bot. Other bots
  are skipped unless `INDEX_BOT_MEDIA=true`.
- Vision uses AnyModel's OpenAI-compatible API with `VISION_API_KEY`; tolerate
  JSON responses wrapped in Markdown code fences.
- Alembic exclusively owns the database schema; commit every revision.
- Never commit or print `.env`, tokens, credentials, media samples, evaluation
  cases, backups, notebooks, or database files.
- Check existing Compose services before starting or recreating them.
- CI rebuilds/tests on `main` pushes and publishes to GHCR on git tags;
  Compose defaults to `ghcr.io/netherquartz/mediaarchivistbot:latest`.
- Every release tag must have a matching GitHub Release with release notes.
- Proactively update this rule and `AGENTS.md` when persistent project context
  changes.
- Run the verification checklist in `AGENTS.md` before claiming readiness.
- Do not commit, restore a database, or recreate a live bot unless the user has
  explicitly authorized that action.
